# pm-copilot — environment configuration
# Copy this file to .env and configure your provider(s).
#
# Two ways to run:
#   1. ZERO-CONFIG (recommended for local dev):
#      Leave every key below blank. Run `pnpm dev`. The web app's setup
#      screen lets you paste keys directly into the browser, encrypted to
#      IndexedDB, and the server proxies LLM calls via the `x-llm-key`
#      header. If `claude --version` works on your shell the server also
#      falls back to a local Claude Code subprocess for free Anthropic.
#   2. SELF-HOST: set the keys below and the server uses them directly.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Primary provider (one of: anthropic | anthropic-cc | openai | google | perplexity | xai | stub)
# - `anthropic-cc` = Claude Code subprocess (no key needed; requires `claude` CLI on PATH)
# - `stub`         = canned responses for offline/CI runs
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
PROVIDER=anthropic

# Anthropic. If unset and `claude --version` works, the server falls back to
# Claude Code subprocess auth (zero-config for local dev).
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# OpenAI
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1

# Google Gemini (also accepted as GEMINI_API_KEY for compatibility)
# GOOGLE_API_KEY=
# GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Perplexity Sonar
# PERPLEXITY_API_KEY=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional enhancement providers
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Perplexity for web-grounded News agent (overrides primary's web search)
# PERPLEXITY_API_KEY=

# xAI / Grok — required to enable the Sentiment agent's live X-search. Without
# this, the agent falls back to training-data sentiment (and the answer is
# annotated so the user knows it's not real-time). Sentiment tab is greyed
# out only when no xAI key is configured AND no fallback profile matches.
# XAI_API_KEY=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Server
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Server port. The web dev server runs on 5173 (Vite default). If `PORT` is
# set to 5173 (e.g. by a parent shell or preview tool) the server treats it
# as a collision and binds 8787 anyway. Use SERVER_PORT to force a value.
PORT=8787
# SERVER_PORT=8787
PM_COPILOT_CONFIG=./mcp.config.json

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Cache
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
CACHE_DIR=.cache
BRIEF_CACHE_TTL_MS=600000
POSITIONS_CACHE_TTL_MS=60000

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CORS (web app origin)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
CORS_ORIGIN=http://localhost:5173

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Admin (cache flush, metrics)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ADMIN_TOKEN=
